          "name": "subtract-function.md",
          "content": "# Plan: Add subtract function to app.js\n\n## Context\n`app.js` (at repo root) currently exports a single pure utility:\n`export const add = (a, b) => a + b;`\nNo tests, no other modules found in this minimal repo.\n\n## Approach\nFollow the existing pattern exactly — add a named arrow-function export alongside `add`. Keep it pure, no validation, to match current style.\n\n## Changes\n\n### 1. `/app.js` (repo root — absolute workspace path: `app.js`)\nAdd after line 1:\n```js\nexport const subtract = (a, b) => a - b;\n```\nResulting file:\n```js\nexport const add = (a, b) => a + b;\nexport const subtract = (a, b) => a - b;\n```\n\nNo other files need to change. No imports/exports to update, no config changes.\n\nAssumption: keep same `(a, b)` signature and implicit return style as `add`.\n\n## Verification\n- Read back `app.js` to confirm both exports present.\n- Run: `node -e \"import('./app.js').then(m => console.log(m.add(2,3), m.subtract(5,3)))\"` — expect `5 2`.\n- Edge cases to sanity-check: `subtract(0,5) === -5`, `subtract(-2,-2) === 0`, floats.\n"
        }
